Short:        One pack: AmigaOS 3.2.3, ready to use
Uploader:     (the Team fills this in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         util/misc
Version:      0.7.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenUp sets up an AmigaOS 3.2.3 installation in one go. Install AmigaOS 3.2.3,
run OpenUp, reboot: graphics on every monitor, networking, MUI programs,
printing, mail, archives and file types all work, with nothing more to read.

It finds what it is running on (a real Amiga with its cards, a PiStorm, or
AmigaChrome) and installs the Open family to match. Anything it replaces is
kept, and one uninstaller puts everything back.

Version 0.7 is for AmigaChrome instances. Its Installer installs, as you
choose:
- OpenSocket: the network, through the x86 or ARM64 cores (bsdsocket.library
  4.2);
- OpenPrint and OpenView: printing to PDF and network printers, and viewing;
- AmigaChrome sharing: the clipboard and files, shared in and out of the
  Amiga, and an optional Send Out icon to drop files on;
- OpenLook: one look for every GadTools program, title bars and borders too
  (Open, Graphite, Ember, Clear or Classic), with a clear screen font and a
  little more room in the title bars; Look in SYS:Prefs changes it (dark by
  the clock, accent, Lite for a real 68040, desktop profiles); its frames
  are drawn through OpenGfx, so OpenLook patches nothing in graphics.library;
- Backgrounds: the look's desktop as Workbench's backdrop, for your screen;
- OpenTypes: which program opens each kind of file (SYS:Prefs/OpenTypes);
- OpenCompress: opens, tests and extracts ADF, ADZ, DMS, LhA, zip, tar and
  gzip, from its window in SYS:Utilities or from the Shell;
- OpenService: services from AmigaChrome's boards and from a Cradle you pair
  with (DEVS:openservice.device, and C:Nursery to list them); nothing goes on
  the network until a Cradle is paired.
- OpenImage: datatypes for WebP and WebM on the Amiga itself, and through
  OpenService for AVIF, HEIC, JPEG XL, camera RAW, SVG, FLAC, Ogg, MP3, MIDI,
  MP4 and other video, and office documents, and music modules: MOD, MED,
  Oktalyzer, DigiBooster, XM, S3M, IT, played on the Amiga itself through
  AHI, with the mixing on another core when there is one;
  datatypes already there stay;
- OpenWindows: windows snap to edges and to each other, Amiga+Tab switches
  between them, a double-click in a title bar brings the window to the
  front, the wheel scrolls the window under the pointer, and programs'
  windows open where they were last left, Workbench drawers too if you like
  (Windows in SYS:Prefs);
- OpenDock: a dock for your programs, starting with ToolManager's, AmiDock's
  or AmiStart's buttons when you have one (Dock in SYS:Prefs);
- OpenUp Setup: a few questions at the next start, and the startup switches;
- OpenMenus: menus in the theme's look, from the screen bar or at the
  pointer, and a menu for each icon and for the desktop on the right button,
  with MagicMenu's settings taken over; the bar can sit at any edge of the
  screen, and the menus work from the keyboard;
- OpenFiles (new): a file manager with two panes and
  tabs, safe copies, a trashcan on each disk and undo (SYS:Utilities);
- OpenPlay (new): a media player for everything the datatypes open, with a
  playlist and a slideshow (SYS:Utilities);
- OpenTitle (new): AmigaChrome's logo, the free chip and fast memory, a
  clock, and a cog at the right end that opens any settings editor, on the
  title bar, set in SYS:Prefs/TitleBar; beside the cog, the taskspace holds
  other programs' icons (Tata's first);
- Sound (new): the volume, Amiga sound (Paula) and AHI sound in one editor,
  and a speaker on the menu bar; the old Sound editor is kept in
  SYS:Prefs/Classic;
- OpenEdit (new): a text editor with tabs, find and replace, and colours
  for scripts and code (C:OpenEdit);
- OpenBlanker (new, always installed): the screen blanker; after five minutes
  without a key or the mouse it plays Gods and Angels, AmigaChrome's homage
  to the people who made the Amiga and kept it alive
  (SYS:Tools/Commodities/OpenBlanker; ENV:OpenPrefs/Blanker sets the seconds);
- OpenWrite (new): a word processor for DOCX, ODT and Amiga documents,
  with PDF export, printing, spelling and an ARexx port
  (SYS:Utilities/OpenWrite), and C:OWConvert for scripts;
- OpenMail (new, a preview, off unless picked): a mail reader for IMAP mail
  over TLS, set up from the address for Gmail, Outlook and others
  (SYS:Utilities/OpenMail); it needs AmiSSL 5 (Aminet util/libs);
- OpenBrowser (new, a preview, off unless picked): a web browser built on
  WebKit, in its own archive, OpenUp-<version>-OpenBrowser.lha, unpacked
  beside the pack; it needs an FPU and is best on a 68040;
- OpenMulticore (new): openmulticore.library, so programs can hand work to
  the other cores of AmigaChrome's cores board (music modules in OpenPlay
  do), or to the main CPU where there is no board;
- OpenMUI (preview, off unless picked): zunemaster.library, MUI built from
  AROS's Zune for OS 3.x, beside MUI and replacing nothing, with ZuneTest
  (SYS:Tools);
- OpenRTG (new, off unless picked): Workbench on OpenRTG's own 16-bit screen
  on AmigaChrome's graphics board, without Picasso96, whose monitor for that
  board is put aside and comes back with the uninstaller. It brings
  openrtg.library 0.13, with opengpu.library 0.9 and the board's driver;
- OpenGPU (new): opengpu.library 0.9, so programs' drawing and SDL 2 games
  run on the x86 or ARM64 cores and GL (Mesa) on the GPU, through
  AmigaChrome's graphics board, and on the Amiga's own CPU where there is no
  board; OpenGfx, the faster graphics.library drawing, is inside it now
  (opengfx.library 1.2 stays for programs that open it); SDL 2 (with
  SDL2_image and SDL2_mixer) and GL are modules in LIBS:OpenGPU, loaded
  once, kept resident and shared by every program that asks; TinyGL
  programs run on GL too (LIBS:tinygl.library), and C:OpenGPUCheck checks
  it;
- Warp3D and MiniGL (new): Warp3D.library 5.0 and minigl.library 29
  (OpenGL 1.1) on OpenGPU, for Warp3D and MiniGL games and programs; they
  need a 68040 or 68060 with its FPU; a Warp3D.library already there
  (Wazp3D's) is kept, and Wazp3D's settings are taken over (C:Warp3DPrefs
  changes them; W3DTest and MGLTest in SYS:Tools show them working);
- Icons (new): Gorilla, AROS's icon set (GPL), as new pictures for the
  system's own drawers, programs and default icons; the old pictures are
  kept and come back with the uninstaller;
- OpenCrypto (new): opencrypto.library 2.0, the sums behind secure
  connections (SSH's key exchanges, host keys, SHA-2, AES), on the x86 or
  ARM64 cores on AmigaChrome and on the Amiga's own CPU elsewhere;
- OpenTLS (new, off unless picked; it comes with OpenFTP): opentls.library,
  secure connections (TLS 1.2) for the Open programs, OpenFTP's FTPS first,
  with its sums through OpenCrypto; the server's certificate is checked
  against Mozilla's list of certificate authorities (S:OpenTLS, MPL-2.0,
  its licence beside it; your own go in ENVARC:OpenTLS/certs);
- OpenPuTTY (new, off unless picked): PuTTY 0.85 for AmigaOS 3.2 on
  OpenCrypto, with SSH, Telnet and serial terminals and key sign-in
  (SYS:Utilities/OpenPuTTY); it brings OpenCrypto with it and needs a
  network stack;
- OpenDemos (new, off unless picked): Boing, Chrome Gears and Copper Tunnel,
  three small 3D demos in GL on OpenGPU (SYS:Utilities/OpenDemos);
- Tata (new, off unless picked while it is 0.x): before a program runs or
  a file opens, Tata checks it against a list of programs and files known
  to crash, draw wrongly or fail on AmigaOS 3.2.3 or with OpenUp
  (S:Tata.known), and asks first; its window is SYS:Prefs/Tata, its icon
  sits on the title bar, and "Tata OFF" in a Shell turns it off;
- OpenFTP (new, off unless picked): FTP and FTPS in two panes, with a site
  manager (SYS:Utilities/OpenFTP); plain FTP works as it is; FTPS works with
  OpenTLS (opentls.library), and AmiSSL 5 is still used if present;
- Unofficial Telegram for Amiga (Open) (new, a preview, off unless picked):
  Telegram chats in a window (SYS:Utilities/UnofficialTelegram); it isn't
  made by Telegram, and it needs setting up first: your own Telegram API key
  (free, from my.telegram.org) and Telegram's service on AmigaChrome's x86 or
  ARM64 cores or a paired Cradle; until then its window says what is missing;
- OpenGPU developer files (new, off unless picked): SDL 2's, SDL 1.2's,
  OpenGL's and GLA's headers and link libraries, with examples, in
  SYS:Developer/OpenGPU-SDK (assign OpenGPU-SDK:), for building programs on
  the Amiga;
- OpenInput (new, off unless picked): openinput.library, game controllers
  for every program in one standard layout, with C:OIList, and Gamepads in
  SYS:Prefs to test and map pads and choose which drives which port (an
  opt-in patch there lets older games see a modern pad); on AmigaChrome it
  sees the Amiga's ports for now.
Workbench's Tools menu gets two sub-menus (new): OpenUp, with the Open
programs that are installed (and OpenUp Update...), and Preferences, with
their settings editors (Look, Windows, Dock, Menus, Title bar, Sound,
OpenTypes, Tata, Gamepads, OpenUp Setup). SYS:C/OpenUpMenu keeps them there; "OpenUpMenu
QUIT" takes them out.
Every file it adds or replaces is listed in ENVARC:OpenAmiga/OpenUp.manifest;
replaced files are kept in SYS:Storage/OpenUp-Superseded; its startup lines
sit in one marked block in S:User-Startup. Uninstall-OpenUp (in
SYS:Utilities/OpenUp) takes it all out again.

